                        "entry_id": "739964a6-9d6f-3ac1-838a-3216f3b1b2c6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A vaulted corridor or arcade at, or just below ground level; normally lit by openings in the upper part of the vault. Also a roofed promenade that is enclosed with side walls that have windows or openings instead of columns."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Roman"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "068d7242-0bf3-45c6-9210-766821a1b0ea",
                                "sense_id": "2f623e7c-9ed7-301d-bb8e-cc9a569bd0f7",
                                "text": "The close walkes, which were called cryptoporticus were not of choice but of necessitie, when extremitie of weather would not let them walke abroad."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
